# Personal Finance Tracker SaaS — Cursor Rules

## Project Identity

- **Name:** Personal Finance Tracker (SaaS PWA)
- **Repo:** saas-personal-finance
- **Stack:** Laravel 13 + Inertia.js + React 19 + Ant Design 5 + ProTable + MySQL 8.4
- **PWA:** Workbox + vite-plugin-pwa (offline-capable, installable, push notifications)
- **Multi-tenant:** Jetstream Teams + Sanctum SPA auth
- **Billing:** Stripe (primary) + Paddle (fallback) via Laravel Cashier
- **External APIs:** Google Cloud Vision (OCR), Deepgram/Whisper (STT), OpenAI GPT-4o-mini (NLP parsing + embeddings), exchangerate-api.com, Google Sheets API v4
- **Queue:** Laravel Horizon (Redis)
- **Testing:** PHPUnit (TDD mandatory) + Laravel Dusk (browser)

## Project Conventions

### Code Organization

```
app/Actions/        → single-action classes, one per business operation, ->execute()
app/Services/       → external API wrappers (Stripe, GoogleVision, Deepgram, OpenAI, GoogleSheets, ExchangeRate)
app/DTOs/           → readonly PHP classes for structured data (TransactionData, OcrResultData)
app/Enums/          → backed string enums (TransactionType, AccountType, Frequency, SubscriptionTier)
app/Jobs/           → queued jobs (OCR, voice, recurring, import, export, AI)
app/Notifications/  → mail + webpush notifications (BillReminderDue, ReportReady)
```

### Naming Conventions

- **DB:** snake_case tables/columns
- **PHP classes:** PascalCase (Controllers, Models, Actions, Services)
- **React components:** PascalCase files, camelCase props/functions
- **Routes:** kebab-case URIs, kebab-case route names
- **Validation:** one FormRequest per write endpoint (Store*Request / Update*Request), no inline $request->validate()

### Multi-Tenancy Pattern

- Every tenant-owned model uses `BelongsToTeam` trait (global scope + auto-fill `team_id`)
- `EnsureTeamContext` middleware on all authenticated routes
- Team switching updates `users.current_team_id` — single source of truth
- Stripe subscriptions are on the `Team` model (Cashier `Billable` trait)

### API Response Envelope

Every API response: `{ data, message, errors, meta }` via JsonResource — never raw `response()->json()`

### React State

- Inertia shared props: `auth.user`, `current_team`, `flash`
- Only 2 global React Contexts: `ThemeContext` (dark/light) and `CurrencyContext` (base currency + rates)
- Everything else: local component state or server state fetched per-page

### Error Handling

- Domain exceptions extend `App\Exceptions\DomainException`
- Exception handler maps to Inertia error bags (web) or JSON envelope (API/XHR)

## Database

- **Database:** saas_personal_finance (MySQL 8.4)
- **Key tables (as they are created):** teams, users, accounts, categories, tags, transactions, budgets, recurring_transactions, saving_goals, goal_contributions, bill_reminders, categorization_rules, ai_categorization_logs, imports, exchange_rates, ocr_jobs, voice_jobs
- **Query preference:** use Eloquent with team scope, never raw SQL unless reporting/aggregation
- **Migrations:** always include indexes, foreign keys, and team_id where applicable

## TDD Workflow (Mandatory)

1. Write failing Feature/Unit test
2. Run test — verify it FAILS
3. Write minimal implementation
4. Run test — verify it PASSES
5. Commit

Tasks marked `[TDD]` in the plan MUST follow this exact flow.

## Git Workflow

- Commit after every completed task
- Commit format: `type: description` (feat:, fix:, refactor:, test:, docs:)
- Push to `main` after each phase completion
- Auto-commit after agent implementation — no need to ask permission

## Documentation Maintenance

After every significant code change, update:

| Change Type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Architecture/structure | `docs/architecture.md` + Mermaid diagrams |
| Feature implementation | `docs/todo.md` (move to completed) |
| Scope/priority change | `docs/backlog.md` |
| Technical decision | `docs/decisions.md` |
| Bug/critical learning | `MEMORY.md` |

### Architecture Docs

- Document CURRENT working state, not intended state
- Include actual database tables/columns as they exist
- Reference real file paths and function names
- Remove deprecated info, don't mark it — just delete it

### Task Management

- Format: `[status] P#: description [files, APIs, context] (completed: YYYY-MM-DD)`
- Status: `[ ]` pending, `[WIP]` in progress, `[blocked]` blocked, `[done]` complete
- Priority: P0 critical, P1 important, P2 nice-to-have, P3 future
- Move completed items to "Recently Completed" section
- Archive old tasks when todo.md gets cluttered

## External Services (API Keys in .env)

| Service | Env Key | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| Stripe | `STRIPE_KEY`, `STRIPE_SECRET` | Subscription billing |
| Paddle | `PADDLE_VENDOR_ID`, `PADDLE_API_KEY` | International billing fallback |
| Google Cloud Vision | `GOOGLE_CLOUD_VISION_KEY` | OCR receipt scanning |
| Deepgram | `DEEPGRAM_API_KEY` | Speech-to-text |
| OpenAI | `OPENAI_API_KEY` | NLP parsing + categorization embeddings |
| ExchangeRate | `EXCHANGERATE_API_KEY` | Currency conversion |
| Google Sheets | `GOOGLE_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS` | Export to Sheets |

## PWA Conventions

- Service worker: `resources/js/sw.js` via Workbox
- Icons: 192x192 + 512x512 maskable in `public/icons/`
- Offline: cache-first for assets, network-first for API, stale-while-revalidate for data
- Camera: `getUserMedia` via React hook, Tesseract.js for client preview
- Microphone: `MediaRecorder` API via React hook
- Push: `laravel-notification-channels/webpush` + VAPID keys

## Phase-by-Phase Approach

This project follows a 10-phase plan (see `docs/2026-07-26_102913-personal-finance-plan.md`). Each phase is self-contained and must be completed (all tests green) before moving to the next. DRY, YAGNI, TDD in every phase.

## Important

- This is a NEW project (not yet launched) — no existing data to preserve
- Dark mode is the default (AntD `ConfigProvider` dark algorithm)
- React state management: Inertia shared props + local state only (no Redux — YAGNI)
- All API responses use `{ data, message, errors, meta }` envelope
- Never use inline validation — always FormRequest classes
- Never use raw SQL for CRUD — always Eloquent with team scope

Remember: These documents should provide comprehensive context for future development and AI assistance, evolving as living documentation that stays current with the codebase.